*** QWEN_RELIABILITY candidate — unconfirmed initial SSE -> unusable end -> sibling failover
*** Source inspected: Ai-b0ss/qwen-free-api@acfb87af4831b6a3846b2edf1e599d20a769529b
*** Target: server.js, non-stream collectNonStream catch/retry block
*** Status: HOSTED_REPRO_CONFIRMED, not yet applied to product branch

Intent
------
Do NOT mark an account merely because gateInitialStream() released an unconfirmed stream on timeout/buffer cap. A legitimate first model frame may simply be slow/large.

Only when collectNonStream() later proves that the entire released stream ended with
`Qwen upstream closed without a usable response`:

1. mark the ACTUAL producing account (`response.account`) as account-local failure once;
2. choose a fresh eligible candidate from `accountStore.candidates()`;
3. prepare the retry for that fresh candidate and call `sendChatRequest(..., retryPreferred)`;
4. if a retry stream itself later ends unusably, mark its ACTUAL `retry.account` once before the next bounded attempt;
5. never reuse another account's upstream chat id (`currentOnly:false` remains mandatory);
6. provider-wide circuit behaviour remains unchanged;
7. do not double-count the initial empty-response failure in the outer generic catch.

Minimal semantic replacement for the existing empty-response retry block
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Before the `try { json = await chatAdapter.collectNonStream(...) }` block, add:

    let initialEmptyResponseClassified = false;

Then replace the current empty-response branch inside `catch (err)` with the following logic:

    if (/^Qwen upstream closed without a usable response/i.test(err.message)) {
      if (response.account) {
        accountStore.markFailure(response.account, err.message);
        initialEmptyResponseClassified = true;
      }

      for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt += 1) {
        const retryPreferred = accountStore.candidates()[0] || null;
        if (!retryPreferred) break;

        const retryPrepared = await preparePublicPayloadGoverned(effectiveBody, {
          currentOnly: false,
          compaction,
          sessionKey,
          headers: req.headers,
          account: retryPreferred,
        });
        const retry = await qwenClient.sendChatRequest(
          retryPrepared.qwenPayload,
          retryPreferred,
        );
        if (!retry.status) continue;

        try {
          json = await chatAdapter.collectNonStream(retry.response, {
            toolParser: retryPrepared.hasTools ? tools.createToolCallStreamParser() : null,
          });
          const saved = sessionStore.set(sessionKey, retry.chatId || retryPrepared.chatId, {
            accountId: retry.account ? retry.account.id : retryPreferred.id,
            awaitingCompactedHistory: compaction,
            toolPromptHash: retryPrepared.toolPromptHash,
            history: sessionStore.checkpointAcceptedToolProgress(
              restoredMessages,
              json?.choices?.[0]?.message,
            ),
          });
          if (!saved) {
            const error = new Error('Accepted non-stream retry tool call checkpoint was rejected');
            error.code = 'QWEN_TOOL_CHECKPOINT_REJECTED';
            throw error;
          }
          return res.json(json);
        } catch (retryError) {
          if (!/^Qwen upstream closed without a usable response/i.test(retryError.message)) {
            throw retryError;
          }
          if (retry.account) accountStore.markFailure(retry.account, retryError.message);
        }
      }
    }

Finally, change the outer generic classification guard from:

    if (!err || err.code !== 'QWEN_TOOL_CHECKPOINT_REJECTED') {
      accountStore.markFailure(response.account, err.message);
    }

to semantics equivalent to:

    if (
      (!initialEmptyResponseClassified || !/^Qwen upstream closed without a usable response/i.test(err.message)) &&
      (!err || err.code !== 'QWEN_TOOL_CHECKPOINT_REJECTED')
    ) {
      accountStore.markFailure(response.account, err.message);
    }

Required regression
-------------------
Offline/hosted, two eligible accounts A/B:

A. initial gate releases `confirmedResponse=false` because of timeout OR buffer cap;
B. released A stream later ends with no usable choices -> collectNonStream throws empty-response;
C. A is marked account-local failure exactly once;
D. next retry prepares and sends with B, not A;
E. B gets a fresh upstream thread / no A chat id reuse;
F. if B also ends empty, B is classified once before any third bounded attempt;
G. a slow/large stream that later yields a real choices frame is NOT classified merely for the unconfirmed release;
H. provider-wide WAF/trust/pressure still stops sibling probing.

Hosted reproduction before patch
--------------------------------
Current retry selection with original `preferredAccount=A` and no local classification produced:
`A -> A -> A`.
After classifying the actual unusable producer A, the next eligible candidate is B.
